    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Headquarters trap: RBI and SEBI are based in Mumbai, whereas IRDAI is in Hyderabad and PFRDA is in New Delhi.",
        "SEBI was initially established as a non-statutory body in 1988 before receiving statutory powers through the SEBI Act, 1992.",
        "PFRDA was established by an executive order in 2003, but its governing act was officially notified later in 2013."
      ],
      "id": "hm5eqyl"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "RBI oversees monetary policy, currency issuance, and banking operations under the RBI Act, 1934.",
        "SEBI regulates stock exchanges, securities transactions, and investor protection via the SEBI Act, 1992.",
        "IRDAI enforces regulations across life and general insurance companies under the IRDA Act, 1999.",
        "PFRDA regulates the National Pension System (NPS) and the pension market in India under the PFRDA Act, 2013.",
        "All four regulatory heads are members of the Financial Stability and Development Council (FSDC) chaired by the Union Finance Minister."
      ],
      "id": "9ckwq78"
    }
